<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's National Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as PNP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> is one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>'s two main political parties, founded in 1938 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-manley">Norman Manley</a> amid labour unrest. Social democratic in outlook, it governed under Manley in the years before independence and has alternated in power with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica-labour-party">Jamaica Labour Party</a> since 1962, under leaders including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-manley">Michael Manley</a> and P. J. Patterson.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-national-party.jpg" alt="People's National Party" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: People's National Party of Jamaica · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:People%27s_National_Party_(Jamaica)_Logo_(2021_-_present).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
